  <wpt lat="50.390042765066028" lon="-105.53502386435866">
    <ele>0</ele>
    <time>2026-06-27T16:54:51Z</time>
    <name>Tunnels of Moose Jaw (Moose Jaw, SK)</name>
    <cmt>&lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/1411/922033219_21edffe20e_b.jpg"
Local Folklore: Popular urban legends claim the tunnels were used by early Chinese immigrants hiding from persecution or by American gangsters—most famously Al Capone—during the Prohibition era for bootlegging. While historical proof for these specific legends is sparse, the lore inspired a major commercial tourist attraction launched in 2000.
Text source = https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moose_Jaw#Museums
Image source = https://www.flickr.com/photos/canadarideforclimate/922033219/</cmt>
    <desc>&lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/1411/922033219_21edffe20e_b.jpg"
